WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.368
A failure taxonomy you can diagnose.

2
00:00:02.648 --> 00:00:12.184
Barnett and colleagues (2024) reported seven failure points from building three RAG systems in research, education, and biomedicine.

3
00:00:12.464 --> 00:00:21.104
This course uses six categories that map onto them and onto the stages you built in weeks 1 to 3, because each category points at a different fix.

4
00:00:21.384 --> 00:00:22.493
Missing content.

5
00:00:22.773 --> 00:00:25.013
The answer isn’t in the corpus at all.

6
00:00:25.293 --> 00:00:31.032
The correct behavior is to abstain, and the failure is answering anyway (Barnett’s FP1).

7
00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:37.221
Fix: abstention, and a log of unanswerable questions so the content owners know what to write.

8
00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:38.589
Retrieval miss.

9
00:00:38.869 --> 00:00:42.133
The answer is in the corpus, but no retriever returned it.

10
00:00:42.413 --> 00:00:51.693
Common causes are vocabulary mismatch (the user says “per diem,” the policy says “meal limit”), chunks that split the answer, and missing metadata.

11
00:00:51.973 --> 00:00:56.453
Fix: hybrid search, query rewriting, better chunking (weeks 2 and 3).

12
00:00:56.733 --> 00:00:57.672
Ranking miss.

13
00:00:57.952 --> 00:01:02.432
Retrieval found the passage but it ranked below the cutoff (Barnett’s FP2).

14
00:01:02.712 --> 00:01:06.979
Fix: reranking, a larger k, or both, measured with recall at k.

15
00:01:07.259 --> 00:01:08.560
Context overflow.

16
00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:18.397
The passage made the cut but was dropped or truncated when the prompt was assembled, because of a token budget or a consolidation step (Barnett’s FP3).

17
00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:23.989
Fix: budget by tokens, not passage count, and log exactly what reached the model.

18
00:01:24.269 --> 00:01:25.443
Synthesis error.

19
00:01:25.723 --> 00:01:40.528
The right passage was in the context and the model still got it wrong: didn’t extract it, merged two facts, answered too generally or too narrowly, left something out, or ignored the requested format (Barnett’s FP4 to FP7).

20
00:01:40.808 --> 00:01:45.395
Fix: prompt structure, quote-first prompting, a different model, verification.

21
00:01:45.675 --> 00:01:46.805
Outdated source.

22
00:01:47.085 --> 00:01:51.160
The answer is faithfully drawn from a passage that is no longer true.

23
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:59.419
Barnett’s list doesn’t name this one, but it’s common in company corpora, and lesson 10’s lab showed that every mechanical check passes it.

24
00:01:59.699 --> 00:02:07.187
Fix: at ingestion (remove or flag superseded documents, store effective dates), and in the prompt (prefer the newest).
